# PSR-4b-whyDenali-docs — narrative SoT alignment

## Prerequisite

[`psr-4b-whyDenali.mdoc`](./psr-4b-whyDenali.mdoc) renamed the **runtime** gate to
`guestLanding.sections.whySection` and dual-reads deprecated `whyDenali`.
Follow-on from that inventory: long-form docs still taught `whyDenali` as current.

## Scope

| Work | Done |
| --- | --- |
| Inventory live narrative docs still teaching `whyDenali` as canonical | Yes |
| Retarget marketing-landing / plan / ADR / design-system / public-catalog | Yes |
| Smoke ratchet over the retargeted set | Yes |
| Expire codegen dual-read of `whyDenali` | **Yes** — see [`psr-4b-whyDenali-alias-expiry.mdoc`](./psr-4b-whyDenali-alias-expiry.mdoc) |
| Rename CSS `data-marketing-home-why*` hooks | **No** (already product-neutral) |
| Rewrite ENTERPRISE_AUDIT_REPORT historical findings | **No** (frozen forensic text) |

## Canonical rule after this wave

| Layer | Token |
| --- | --- |
| Manifest / generated SDK | `whySection` |
| Docs teaching current contract | `whySection` |
| Codegen dual-read | **expired** — `whyDenali` key fail-closed |
| CSS hooks | `data-marketing-home-why` (unchanged) |

## Ratchet

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-4b-whyDenali-docs-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-4b-whyDenali-smoke.mjs
```

Land commit: `6b3dd6bf`

## Explicit non-goals

- Removing deprecated alias acceptance in `guest-catalog.mjs`
- CSS selector renames
- Changing marketing React props beyond what prior whyDenali wave already did
